{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123897","id":4657762554,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFZ_Q-g","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123897","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123897.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123897.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123897","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123897/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123897/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123897/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/133c41773e9e6eb6ac4090e74dbe6c9979f348cf","number":123897,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix Inspector Menu Shortcut Crash","user":{"login":"nklbdev","id":7024016,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQwMTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7024016?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/nklbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nklbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123896\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe Inspector dock's \"resource extra\" `MenuButton` popup (New Resource / Load\r\nResource / Save / Save As / Edit Resource from Clipboard / Copy Resource /\r\nShow in FileSystem / Open Documentation / Make Resource Built-In) has several\r\nitems bound to a keyboard shortcut. `MenuButton::shortcut_input()` correctly\r\nchecks `PopupMenu::is_item_disabled()` before running the bound action, via\r\n`PopupMenu::activate_item_by_event()` -- but that check only reflects\r\nwhatever disabled state was last written to that specific item.\r\n\r\nMost items (Save, Save As, Copy Resource, Make Resource Built-In, Open\r\nDocumentation) already had their disabled state recomputed on every Inspector\r\nselection change, in `InspectorDock::update()`. \"Show in FileSystem\" and\r\n\"Edit Resource from Clipboard\" were the exception: their disabled state was\r\nonly recomputed when the popup was actually opened\r\n(`_prepare_resource_extra_popup()`, tied to the button's `about_to_popup`\r\nsignal). So a pure keyboard shortcut press, without ever opening the popup\r\nfor the current selection, could activate \"Show in FileSystem\" while it was\r\nactually invalid for the current selection (for example, while the Inspector\r\nis showing a `Node` rather than a `Resource`) -- crashing with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: Condition \"current_res.is_null()\" is true.\r\n   at: _menu_option_confirm (editor/docks/inspector_dock.cpp:108)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n- Adds a single `_is_menu_option_enabled(int p_option)` predicate, the one\r\n  place that decides whether a given resource-extra-popup option is valid\r\n  right now.\r\n- Uses it to compute every relevant item's disabled state, via a small\r\n  `_update_resource_extra_popup_items()` helper that iterates the popup's\r\n  own items (`get_item_count()` / `get_item_id()`) rather than hand-listing\r\n  option IDs a second time -- called from both `update()` (on every\r\n  selection change) and `_prepare_resource_extra_popup()` (on popup open),\r\n  so all items are now refreshed consistently and at the same two points.\r\n- Calls it again as an early-return guard at the very top of\r\n  `_menu_option_confirm()`, so none of these options can actually run while\r\n  invalid, regardless of what any `PopupMenu` item's disabled flag happens\r\n  to say at the moment it's invoked -- closing the gap described above for\r\n  good, rather than only for this one option.\r\n\r\nI tested this by assigning a keyboard shortcut to \"Property Editor > Show in\r\nFileSystem\" in Editor Settings, selecting a plain `Node` in a scene (so the\r\nInspector shows a `Node`, not a `Resource`), and pressing the shortcut\r\nwithout ever opening the popup first. Before this PR, that reliably crashed\r\nwith the error above; after, it's a silent no-op, matching the item's own\r\n(now consistently up to date) disabled appearance.\r\n\r\n### Use of AI\r\n\r\nI used Claude (Anthropic's AI coding assistant, via Claude Code) throughout\r\nthis fix: to search and read the relevant engine source\r\n(`MenuButton::shortcut_input`, `PopupMenu::activate_item_by_event`,\r\n`InspectorDock::update()` / `_prepare_resource_extra_popup()`) and pin down\r\nthe exact root cause described above, to draft the `_is_menu_option_enabled()`\r\n/ `_update_resource_extra_popup_items()` refactor, and to iterate on\r\nsimplifying it (e.g. replacing a hand-written list of option IDs with\r\niterating the popup's actual items). I reviewed, tested, and adjusted the\r\nresulting change myself before opening this PR; the final code and the\r\nanalysis above are my own understanding of the bug, not taken as-is from the\r\nassistant.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/l